{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["And the verse's saying <b>for all the signs, etc.</b> — it follows from what is written above: ״יְדָעוֹ ה׳ פָּנִים אֵל פָּנִים״ (HaShem knew him face to face) — for all the signs, meaning for the need of the signs etc., and the intent is that for every sign and wonder that HaShem sent him to perform, He would know him face to face." "<b>Further,</b> it may be explained according to what the Rambam wrote in Hilkhot De'ot, that a prophet who arises in Israel need not perform great wonders like those that Moses performed, but any sign at all of the wonders that he performs etc. suffices. And you will find that the Torah stated the strength of faith in Moses in two places: first, at the sea, as it is written (Exodus 14:31): ״וַיַּאֲמִינוּ בַה׳ וּבְמֹשֶׁה עַבְדּוֹ״; second, at the giving of the Torah, as it is written (Exodus 19:9): ״וְגַם בְּךָ יַאֲמִינוּ לְעוֹלָם״." "<b>And see</b> what I explained in the verse ״דַּבֵּר אַתָּה עִמָּנוּ וְנִשְׁמָעָה״ (Exodus 20:16), where I explained וְנִשְׁמָעָה as וּנְקַבְּלָה (and we will accept) — that they had already validated his prophecy with a validation that was palpable and revealed to them. And therefore the word of HaShem came and said: ״וְלֹא קָם נָבִיא עוֹד בְּיִשְׂרָאֵל״ etc." "<b>The reason</b> is that Moses performed all the signs — something no other prophet does — and he did not need to perform all of them. Further, <b>״for all the mighty hand״</b> — that is the splitting of the Sea of Reeds, through which they believed; <b>״and for all the great awe״</b> — that is the standing at Mount Sinai, through which they completed their faith. No other prophet will arise who does such things." "<b>And he concluded</b> by saying ״לְעֵינֵי כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל״ — meaning that they themselves saw these things, and not by way of faith in the manner done with the rest of the prophets who came after him, but with their own eyes they saw that Moses is the true prophet of HaShem and his Torah is the Torah of the <b>living</b> Elohim, truth." "<b>Thus is concluded the parashah of Vezot HaBerakhah.</b>"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:22:53.956101660Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}